  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2509.22592v4</id>
    <title>OT-MeanFlow3D: Bridging Optimal Transport and Meanflow for Efficient 3D Point Cloud Generation</title>
    <updated>2026-10-17T06:52:48Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.22592v4" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.22592v4" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Flow-matching models have recently emerged as a powerful framework for generative modeling, including 3D point cloud synthesis. However, their deployment is limited by the need for multiple sequential sampling steps at inference time. MeanFlow enables single-step generation by learning an average velocity field, but its quality depends heavily on the geometry of the training pairs. In this work, we propose an Optimal Transport-enhanced MeanFlow framework (OT-MF3D) for efficient and accurate 3D point cloud generation and completion. Beyond incorporating OT into MeanFlow, our method introduces a latent-conditioned training algorithm that decouples shape-level sampling from point-level matching. This enables exact point-level OT within each conditioned shape while performing shape-level transport in a compact latent space, avoiding the expensive nested OT computation in point-cloud space. Experiments on standard benchmarks show improved generation and completion quality over fast baselines, with substantially reduced training and inference costs compared with diffusion and other flow-based models.</summary>
    <category term="cs.LG" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2025-09-26T17:12:19Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.LG"/>
    <author>
      <name>Elaheh Akbari</name>
    </author>
